The Mojo standard library for Dolly programs and WebGPU kernels.
Against github.com/modular/modular at the tag mojo/v1.1.0; apply with patch -p1.
Dolly's values are those a C probe printed when compiled by Dolly's cc.

sys/info.mojo
  CompilationTarget.is_dolly(), a dolly column in platform_map, is_webgpu()
  and is_gpu() for the kernel target.
sys/_libc_errno.mojo
  Dolly's libc numbers errors as WASI does, so every ErrNo has a dolly value,
  also those Linux and macOS share. errno is __errno_location, as on Linux.
io/file.mojo, time/time.mojo, ffi/__init__.mojo, os/os.mojo
  Open flags, clock ids, dlopen flags, C long and struct dirent are as on
  Linux. Without these lines a target that is not Linux took macOS's values.
os/_dolly.mojo (new), os/fstat.mojo, os/path/path.mojo
  struct stat as Dolly's libc lays it out, through stat and lstat.
io/file_descriptor.mojo, io/file.mojo, os/os.mojo
  read, write, lseek and mkdir were called with an Int where C has an int or
  mode_t.
  Wasm types every call, so such a call traps; on x86-64 and arm64 the
  register hid it.
_gpu/primitives/id.mojo
  thread_idx, block_idx, block_dim and grid_dim of a WebGPU kernel are calls
  the target prints as WGSL builtins.
io/io.mojo, builtin/debug_assert.mojo, os/os.mojo, sys/__init__.mojo
  A WGSL kernel has nowhere to print. A print is a call the target refuses
  when the kernel can reach it; a failed assert and an abort end the
  invocation without their message.

